From 726a10cd4fbdaf037e049abd334fc7ffdfe33102 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:36:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Prediction computed by kernels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With the inner forces and the tangent operator computed by kernels, the
operator of the prediction is assembled by kernels in a local matrix
kept between the predictions (same pattern as the tangent operator),
and the inner forces at the beginning of the time step are computed by
kernels, instead of the bilinear and linear forms assembled by the
element loops of MFEM: the prediction no longer reads the arrays of the
materials on the host. The linear system is formed as by
FormLinearSystem of MFEM, the essential degrees of freedom being
eliminated in place (EliminateBC with a unit diagonal, the right hand
side being B = Pᵀ b - K X, then B[e] = X[e]). The contributions of the
boundary conditions to the right hand side (imposed pressure...) are
still assembled by MFEM; the prediction is computed as before if they
contribute to the operator, or in sequential with a non conforming
mesh.

The list of the essential degrees of freedom of the prediction is now
allocated by MFEM: an array wrapping the memory of a std::vector can't
be read on the debug device.

Beam (111843 unknowns, 3 steps, 1 process, GPU): 1.81 s instead of
6.25 s, the prediction taking 0.51 s instead of 4.80 s.
